  "findings": [
    "All six outputs are executable under the adapter's original operations interface, but only two repair their focal error correctly and with sufficient citations.",
    "Both owner repairs are omitted. The English owner case also misses a newly added qualifier despite returning syntactically valid empty operations.",
    "The Chinese withdrawal and uncertainty examples succeed; the English withdrawal repair is omitted, and the English uncertainty example executes an unsupported withdrawal.",
    "A native-interface semantic failure on four selected training examples means the audit schema change is not the sole explanation for those local repair failures. These are different inputs from the audit ablation and do not measure the schema effect in isolation.",
    "One successful Chinese withdrawal output differs in wording from its canonical completion but preserves the meaning and is scored correct; canonical matching is only descriptive.",
    "All six end on configured EOS 151645 without reaching the token cap."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All six examples were present in training and were selected by a frozen first-eligible-row rule; they are exposed examples, not held-out generalization data.",
    "Six examples do not estimate full training-set fit or establish underfitting, overfitting, language-group differences, or a specific optimizer/data cause.",
    "There is no base-only arm on these same six native training inputs; native errors cannot uniquely be attributed to the adapter.",
    "Selection and labels are synthetic and AI-reviewed; independent human gold is unavailable.",
    "Keep this six-input local-fit diagnostic separate from the twelve-input adapter-off audit comparison; their denominators and input tasks differ."
  ],
